<section class="page-intro wrap"><h1>Developers</h1><p>Create a plugin or share a theme. The SDK, examples and file formats live alongside the code on GitHub.</p></section><section class="wrap docs-layout"><nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Developers. topics"><a href="#plugins">Plugin SDK</a><a href="#preview-behavior">Preview behavior</a><a href="#themes">Theme development</a></nav><div class="status-content"><article id="plugins"><h2>Plugin SDK</h2><p>The SDK is part of the GitHub source tree. It includes the C API, its implementation, HelloWorld and ARexx examples, build rules and a package validator.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/sdk/README.md">Plugin SDK documentation ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/sdk/Beam68PluginSDK.guide">AmigaGuide manual ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/tree/main/sdk/Example">Example plugins ↗</a></p><ul><li>Protocol 1 is the first public protocol. All bundled native plugins return up to eight selectable text, path or query rows in one message.</li><li>Use the SDK to validate hex input and deliver replies to the launcher. ARexx scripts use the documented atomic text transport. Keep previews quick and free of side effects.</li><li>Ship one drawer with an executable and one manifest, including a stable ID, independent plugin version, trigger and drawer-relative command. Plugin versions are separate from the Beam68 app version: start a new plugin at 0.1 and increment it whenever its implementation changes.</li><li>Run the SDK packaging tool to validate the package. Users install it through Preferences → Plugins → Import. Bundled plugins can be disabled but cannot be removed; third-party plugins can be removed.</li></ul><p>Plugins run as native code. Capability labels describe behavior; they do not restrict access. Document dependencies and test on supported AmigaOS systems.</p></article>
<article id="preview-behavior"><h2>Preview behaviour</h2><p>Users can disable automatic previews per plugin or set an exact delay in Preferences. Beam68 bounds outstanding requests, reserves capacity for manual actions and discards replies belonging to older queries.</p><p>Keep previews quick and free of side effects. Downloads, file changes and other actions should require an explicit user choice. Use Aminet Browser as a bundled example of package details and confirmed downloads.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/tree/main/Plugins/AminetBrowser">Aminet Browser source ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/docs/AREXX.md">Automation and request diagnostics ↗</a></p></article>
<article id="themes"><h2>Theme format</h2><p>Themes use a portable text format rather than a compiled SDK. Start with a bundled file or export a theme from Preferences, edit its colors and import it again.</p><pre><code>#NAME=My Theme
#AUTHOR=Your Name
BEAM68THEME=1
COLORS=FFB000,6B4A00,FFB000,1A1200,140E00</code></pre><p>Each color is a six-digit RGB value. The order is text, shadow, selection fill, selection text and background. Comment metadata can describe the author, name and version. Keep foregrounds readable against both backgrounds. Every theme is editable in Preferences, with an independent saved palette and a Restore original palette control. Mocha is the default; Rose is the reddish built-in theme.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/tree/main/themes">Bundled theme examples ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/src/theme_file.c">Theme file reader and writer ↗</a></p></article>
</div></section>
